---
description: Safe Zoho Sprints MCP operations using Admin/Developer role policy
alwaysApply: false
---

When using Zoho Sprints MCP, follow `skills/zoho-sprints/SKILL.md` and the matching role policy in `policies/`.

- Discover real MCP tools and schemas; never invent a tool or ID.
- Developer: show only stories assigned to the configured user and assigned work in active sprints.
- Create a child Task/Bug only beneath a User Story assigned to the configured user.
- Create a new story only in an active sprint and only when current time is within the inclusive sprint date range.
- Search all relevant active sprints for duplicate/overlapping stories before creating.
- Pause and warn on likely duplicates.
- Verify every successful mutation by reading the record again when possible.
- Do not claim success if the tool is missing or the operation fails.


## Git Change Audit
For local Git-to-Zoho reconciliation, follow `workflows/git-change-audit.md` and `workflows/git-change-ledger.md`. Read the local checkpoint and pending queue first, refresh prior Zoho item statuses, process only unaccounted changes, check duplicates, respect current-user assignment and inclusive sprint date windows, default to dry-run, verify writes, and never blindly retry an ambiguous create.
